      "summary": "PLP UI - Bottom Zone (Editorial Slots)",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \n\n\nI want\n the bottom of the product listing page to surface relevant editorial content,\n\n\nso that\n my browsing experience feels curated and I can continue exploring beyond the product grid.\nReference image (Figma is leading):\nBelow the product grid and \"Load More\" button, the PLP bottom zone is a configurable area that can vary by category. It is not a fixed layout — it is a set of component slots that a Site Merchandiser maintains. \nThis story covers the component shells; content authoring in Contentful will be part of another user story.\nPLP Bottom components as per design:\nFull-width editorial image block\n — a full-bleed image with caption text, pagination dots, and a \"Next\" CTA linking to another collection or editorial page. Functions as a campaign or collection crosslink.\nEditorial feature block\n — a named editorial story (e.g. \"Birds in Motion\") with a large image on the left, an optional product tile on the right, a title, description, and a \"More\" CTA. Links through to an editorial or collection page.\nTwo-column content block\n — two side-by-side editorial panels, each with an image, title, description, and a CTA link (e.g. \"In the Details\" linking to editorial content; \"Find a Boutique\" linking to the store locator). Panels are independently configurable.\nNo editorial slot\n  — some PLPs will have nothing between the grid and Recently Viewed.",
