{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "349437965",
    "title": "[DRAFT] TSD: SFCC MRT API Capabilities (Spike SFCC-122)",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/349437965",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "> **DRAFT: for squad review, not final.** Authored by Marcel Angelo Navarro for spike SFCC-122. Two items are still open pending a session with M. Ramachandran (see section 6, Open questions). Please review; do not treat this as authoritative until this notice is removed and the page is marked final.\n\n**Spike deliverable, Squad-A**\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| Jira | SFCC-122 (Spike, High, In Progress) |\n| Assignee | Marcel Angelo Navarro |\n| Reporter | Jasmijn Tsang |\n| Related | SFCC-121 (Validate MuleSoft Sync), SFCC-123 (Contentful design), SFCC-1 (Platform Setup & Environments, owner: M. Ramachandran) |\n| Status of this doc | Draft for squad review |\n| Last updated | 2026-07-22 |\n\n---\n\nTL;DR\n-----\n\n1. **\"MRT\" is the hosting and proxy layer, not an API.** Managed Runtime is the PWA Kit Node server. The APIs the storefront actually consumes for product, category, and pricing data are **SCAPI (Salesforce Commerce API, the Shopper APIs)**, reached *through* the MRT proxy.\n2. **SCAPI can already serve product, category, and pricing today.** The capability exists now: `shopper-products`, `shopper-search`, and pricebook-aware pricing are wired and proven in this codebase. Standalone `shopper-promotions` is available through the base template and is demonstrated here via `expand=promotions`.\n3. **The blocker is empty data, not a missing API.** Product and price data are absent from the lower environments because the source-to-SFCC data feeds have not been built yet: product/catalogue is AP21 to MuleSoft to SFCC, and price is AP21 to SFCC via XML pricebook import (mechanism, SFTP / API / MuleSoft, still to be confirmed). That is a data-population problem, owned server-side, not an MRT or SCAPI capability gap.\n4. **MuleSoft does not serve product or pricing to the PWA.** The direct PWA to MRT to MuleSoft path is only for orders, returns, and real-time boutique stock. Product and price master data is a separate server-to-server import into SFCC.\n5. **To unblock lower-environment build and test now:** load catalogue and pricebook data into the `bkzk-002` sandbox (Business Manager or the OCAPI Data API), confirm the BM site, catalogue, and pricebook assignment, then the PWA consumes it via SCAPI with no code change.\n\n---\n\n1. Objective\n------------\n\nDocument the SFCC MRT (Managed Runtime) APIs relevant to the Zimmermann storefront build, so the squad has a clear picture of what is available for product, pricing, and category data consumption before MuleSoft is ready. This lets the squad determine what can be built and tested in lower environments in the meantime.\n\n2. Background\n-------------\n\n* Base Business Manager configuration is in place on the SFCC sandbox, but product and price data are currently missing because MuleSoft is not yet ready.\n* Understanding the MRT API capabilities tells the squad what can be built and tested in lower environments while that feed is being built.\n* A session is to be set up with M. Ramachandran (owner of SFCC-1, Platform Setup & Environments) to confirm the sandbox data-loading approach.\n* The storefront is a PWA Kit application (`zimmermann-pwa`) hosted on Managed Runtime, template-extending `@salesforce/retail-react-app`, consuming commerce data from SFCC and editorial content from Contentful.\n\n3. Tasks and findings\n---------------------\n\n### 3.1 Task 1: Review and document the available MRT APIs\n\n**How commerce data reaches the storefront.** The browser talks to SFCC through a proxy hosted by Managed Runtime. Nothing calls SFCC directly from a hard-coded backend host; every call goes through an MRT proxy path, which lets MRT attach server-only credentials and keeps secrets out of the browser bundle.\n\nnonewide760Browser (React, SSR + CSR)\n| @salesforce/commerce-sdk-react (TanStack Query under the hood)\nv\nMRT proxy /mobify/proxy/api --> SCAPI (Shopper APIs): product, category, price, search, promotions, basket, orders, customers\n/mobify/proxy/ocapi --> OCAPI (configured; fallback for gaps; not currently called from app code)\n/mobify/proxy/mulesoft --> MuleSoft (orders, returns, boutique stock ONLY; designed, not yet wired)\nv\nSFCC realm (sandbox bkzk-002 in Dev)\n\nThe single SDK `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` (v5.2.0) handles every SFCC call: SLAS token lifecycle, retry, and TanStack Query caching. Verified in `overrides/app/components/_app-config/index.tsx` (CommerceApiProvider wiring) and consumed via hooks such as `useProduct` and `useProductSearch`.\n\n#### 3.1.1 SCAPI Shopper APIs (primary path for product, category, pricing)\n\nReached at MRT proxy path `/mobify/proxy/api` (`config/default.js:131`). These are the APIs that serve the data this spike is about.\n\n| API family | Path root | Serves | Verbs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Shopper Products | `/product/shopper-products/v1/*` | Product detail, master/variant resolution, images, prices on the product | GET |\n| Shopper Search | `/search/shopper-search/v1/*` | Category product listing (`cgid` refinement), keyword search, faceting, sort, suggestions | GET |\n| Shopper Promotions | `/pricing/shopper-promotions/v1/*` | Active promotions, coupon validation | GET |\n| Shopper Login (SLAS) | `/checkout/shopper-login/oauth2/*` | Guest and registered auth, token lifecycle | GET, POST |\n| Shopper Baskets | `/checkout/shopper-baskets/v2/*` | Basket / cart lifecycle, line items | GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE |\n| Shopper Orders | `/checkout/shopper-orders/v1/*` | Order placement and lookup of the just-placed order (SFCC-owned checkouts). Order history and detail come from MuleSoft, not SCAPI (see 3.1.6) | POST, GET |\n| Shopper Customers | `/customer/shopper-customers/v1/*` | Profile, addresses, saved-payment references | GET, POST, PATCH |\n\nSource: `.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md` section 4.\n\n**Pricing is fully supported through SCAPI.** The canonical query in the codebase (`overrides/app/pages/home/index.tsx:52-58`) uses `useProductSearch` with `refine: ['cgid=<categoryId>', 'htype=master']` and `expand: ['promotions','variations','prices','images','custom_properties']`, `perPricebook: true`, `allVariationProperties: true`. This demonstrates category refinement plus pricebook-aware pricing and promotion expansion working end to end, given data exists.\n\n#### 3.1.2 Endpoint structure, base URL, and environments\n\n* **SCAPI base host:**`{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com`, proxied via `/mobify/proxy/api`. Verified: `config/default.js:210` host `qmyt7hks.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com`.\n* **Instance identifiers** (non-secret; injected from env into the SDK provider at `config/default.js:132-137`):\n* `shortCode`: `qmyt7hks`\n* `organizationId`: `f_ecom_bkzk_002` (realm/instance `bkzk_002`)\n* `siteId`: `ZimmermannAU` (default). The app defines 10 PWA storefront sites backed by 7 distinct SFCC sites (the four EU-domestic locales share SFCC site `ZimmermannEU`); see `config/sites.overlay.js`.\n* `clientId`: SLAS client ID (public identifier, held in `COMMERCE_API_CLIENT_ID`)\n* **Per-environment config:**`config/dev.js`, `test.js`, `sit.js`, `staging.js`, `uat.js`, `production.js` each override `proxyConfigs`. The SCAPI host stays constant (`qmyt7hks...`); the OCAPI host changes per tier (Dev to `bkzk-002.dx...`, Prod to `production-ap01-zimmermann.demandware.net`).\n* **Env switching:**`npm run env -- <tier>` (`scripts/switchEnv.mjs`); deploy per tier via `npm run push:<tier>`, which runs `pwa-kit-dev push -t <target>`.\n* MRT environment variables are managed per environment in the Managed Runtime console and rotated independently of the codebase (Confluence: Technical Solution Design, PWA).\n\n#### 3.1.3 Authentication\n\n* **SLAS private-client flow** issues a guest access token (anonymous shopper, refreshed silently) and a registered shopper token (after email/password login). Tokens are JWTs carrying customer ID, unique shopper ID (USID), and a refresh token.\n* **Secrets stay server-side.** The SLAS client secret is an MRT environment variable and never reaches the browser; the authorisation-code exchange is proxied through the MRT private-client endpoint. The SLAS client ID and SCAPI short code remain in the bundle as public identifiers. Confirmed in `overrides/app/ssr.js:52` (`useSLASPrivateClient: true`) and `overrides/app/components/_app-config/index.tsx:132,147-148`.\n* **Refresh tokens** live in `httpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite=Strict` cookies set by the SSR layer; browser JavaScript never sees the raw refresh token.\n* **Multi-site tokens are channel-scoped.** A token for one site is not valid for another; a storefront switch triggers a fresh server-side authorisation (SLAS Trusted System on Behalf).\n\nSource: `.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md` section 3.\n\n#### 3.1.4 Payload format and query conventions\n\n* **Format:** JSON over HTTPS (TLS 1.2+), standard SCAPI response envelopes.\n* **Every request carries** site ID, organisation ID, locale, currency, and the SLAS bearer token.\n* **Efficiency levers used:**`expand=` to pull promotions/variations/prices/images in one call; `fields=` projection to trim payloads; `perPricebook: true` for pricebook-aware pricing; TanStack Query dedup and caching (documented working targets: catalogue stale time ~60s, promotions ~30s, basket 0s, per `01-sfcc.md` section 6; the app-level default `staleTime` is 10s).\n\n#### 3.1.5 OCAPI (configured proxy; not currently consumed in app code)\n\n* A proxy path `/mobify/proxy/ocapi` is configured (`config/default.js:213-216`, Dev host `bkzk-002.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com`) so that any operation not covered by SCAPI can be proxied through MRT with OCAPI credentials held server-side. No OCAPI credentials ever reach the browser.\n* Current state: OCAPI is **not called from application code**; it is referenced only in host-validation and sync tooling (`scripts/switchEnv.mjs`, `scripts/sfcc/*.mjs`). It is a configured capability held in reserve, not an active runtime dependency.\n* Note the distinction from the import channel below: the **admin OCAPI Data API** used to load catalogue data (3.1.8) is a separate, admin-authenticated channel, not the shopper-facing `/mobify/proxy/ocapi` storefront proxy.\n\n#### 3.1.6 MuleSoft-direct reads via MRT (not product, category, or pricing)\n\nThere is a designed direct path `PWA to MRT to MuleSoft` at `/mobify/proxy/mulesoft/...` for a small set of reads where SFCC adds nothing to the round-trip. It is **scaffolded but not yet wired**: no `mulesoft` entry exists in any `config/*.js`, and the intended mechanism is a server-side `fetch()` from `ssr.js` over a dedicated undici connection pool (`overrides/app/ssr/connectionPools.ts:42-46`, `mulesoftPool`), not a PWA Kit `proxyConfig`. A plain proxyConfig would not suffice, because this path must inject `client_id`/`client_secret` request headers and a session-derived `customer_id` that proxyConfigs cannot add.\n\nIn scope for this path: order history list, order detail, returns, real-time boutique stock (Find in Boutique / BOPIS), GiveX balance check. **Product, category, and pricing are explicitly out of scope for this path.** Source: `.docs/integration/03-mulesoft.md`.\n\n#### 3.1.7 Einstein recommendations (adjacent capability)\n\nPersonalised recommendations use the Einstein API (`config/default.js:140-148`, host `https://api.cquotient.com`), consent-gated, with a static SFCC merchandising-group fallback. Not part of the core product/category/pricing consumption but available through the same app.\n\n#### 3.1.8 Catalogue and pricebook population path (server-to-server, the missing piece)\n\nThis is what \"MuleSoft is not yet ready\" refers to, and it is not an MRT capability at all:\n\n* **Product:** AP21 (ERP, system of record) to MuleSoft (transform to SFCC Catalog XML) to SFCC, delivered via the **admin OCAPI Data API** (`/s/-/dw/data/v*/catalogs`) or SFTP + import job. Per the Confluence TSD, a master catalogue plus per-site storefront catalogues.\n* **Price:** AP21 to SFCC pricebooks, per-site and per-currency, loaded as SFCC Pricebook XML (`pricebook.xsd`). Per the TSD, **there is no direct MuleSoft price integration today**; the delivery mechanism (SFTP / API / MuleSoft) is still to be confirmed (TSD Price open item 1). Pricebook IDs follow `{site}-{currency}-list-prices` and `{site}-{currency}-sale-prices` (e.g. `au-aud-list-prices`, `au-aud-sale-prices`; sale pricebook parents the list pricebook). Import via `sfcc-ci instance:import` or Business Manager Site Import.\n* Product IDs (per TSD): master = `stylecode` (e.g. `4673TS251`); variant = `stylecode + colourcode + sizecode`.\n* The master-catalogue-to-storefront-category assignment is set in Business Manager and cannot be set via XML import.\n* **Catalogue ID caveat:** the TSD names the master as `zimmermann-catalog` and storefront catalogues as `zimmermann-<site>-storefront-catalog`. The PWA repo does not contain SFCC catalogue configuration (that lives in the SFCC cartridge repo), so these IDs are expected to be absent here; that absence is not a contradiction. The only similar-looking value in the repo, `storefront-catalog-eu`, is the `shop.id` field inside a sample MuleSoft order-response payload (`.docs/vendor/mulesoft.md`), not an SFCC catalogue definition. Confirm the actual sandbox catalogue IDs with M. Ramachandran before using them for BM configuration.\n\nSource: Confluence \"TSD: Product, SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration\" and \"TSD: Price, SFCC Pricebooks & Global-e\".\n\n### 3.2 Task 2: Which MRT APIs can serve product, category, and pricing in lower environments now\n\n**Answer: SCAPI can, as soon as data exists in the sandbox.** The API capability is not the constraint. `shopper-products`, `shopper-search` (with `cgid` category refinement), and pricebook-aware pricing via `expand=prices` with `perPricebook=true` all work against any populated SFCC instance.\n\nThe only thing missing in the lower environments is **data in the SFCC catalogue and pricebooks**. Once data is loaded (see section 4), front-end development and testing can proceed against SCAPI with no dependency on the upstream data feeds being finished.\n\n| Capability | Available in lower env now? | Depends on |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Product detail (`shopper-products`) | Yes, once catalogue data is loaded | Sandbox catalogue populated |\n| Category listing / search (`shopper-search`, `cgid`) | Yes, once catalogue + storefront categories + search index exist | BM catalogue assignment + search index rebuild |\n| Pricing (`prices`, `perPricebook`) | Yes, once pricebooks are loaded and assigned | Sandbox pricebooks populated + assigned to site |\n| Promotions (`shopper-promotions`) | Yes, once promotions are configured in BM | BM promotion setup |\n| Auth (SLAS) | Yes, working now | SLAS client already configured |\n\n### 3.3 Task 3: Limitations and gaps to be covered by MuleSoft (or elsewhere)\n\n* **No catalogue or price data in the sandbox** until either sample/manual data is loaded or the source-to-SFCC product and price feeds are built (dependency: SFCC-121).\n* **Catalogue/price freshness and delta handling** (event vs scheduled, sale-price removal signals) are data-feed concerns, not SCAPI concerns.\n* **MuleSoft real-time rate limits** for the direct-read path are unconfirmed (Confluence \"MuleSoft Integration, Open Questions\", item G3).\n* **Delivery mechanism for catalogue import** (OCAPI Data API vs SFTP + import job) and the feed trigger are still open (Confluence TSD Product, open item 1).\n* **Per-environment SLAS client ID / short code** for non-Dev tiers partly outstanding (`.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md` section 7).\n* The **MuleSoft direct-read path** (`/mobify/proxy/mulesoft`) is not yet wired, so order history, returns, and boutique stock are not consumable from the PWA until it is added and MuleSoft endpoints are provisioned per environment.\n\n### 3.4 Task 4: Permanent architecture vs current-state workaround\n\n| Element | Classification | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SCAPI via MRT proxy for product / category / pricing consumption | **Permanent** | The storefront's supported model for all shopper data |\n| SLAS private-client auth via MRT | **Permanent** | Standard PWA Kit pattern |\n| AP21 to MuleSoft to SFCC product/catalogue feed (population) | **Permanent** | The intended catalogue data source; not yet built |\n| AP21 to SFCC price feed via pricebook XML import (population) | **Permanent** | No direct MuleSoft price integration per TSD; mechanism (SFTP / API / MuleSoft) to be confirmed; not yet built |\n| OCAPI via MRT for operations SCAPI does not cover | **Permanent (semi)** | Configured fallback by design; currently unused; shrinks as SCAPI coverage grows |\n| PWA to MRT to MuleSoft direct reads (orders, returns, boutique stock) | **Permanent** | Designed, not yet wired |\n| Manual / sample catalogue and pricebook load into the sandbox | **Workaround** | Current-state only, to unblock lower-env build and test before the permanent product and price feeds exist |\n\n4. Recommended actions to unblock lower environments\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n1. **Load catalogue and pricebook data into the** `bkzk-002` **sandbox.** Options, in order of preference for a quick unblock: - Import a sample/seed catalogue via the **admin OCAPI Data API** (`/s/-/dw/data/v*/catalogs`) or a site-archive import job in Business Manager. - Load pricebooks as SFCC Pricebook XML via `sfcc-ci instance:import` or Business Manager Site Import; IDs follow `{site}-{currency}-list-prices` / `-sale-prices` (e.g. `au-aud-list-prices`). - Note: the catalogue/data tooling and sample data are **not in** `zimmermann-pwa` (the PWA repo only consumes). Per the TSD, the conversion/seed tooling is assumed to live in a separate SFCC cartridge repo (referred to as `zimmermann-sfccworkplace`); confirm the repo name, ownership, and access with M. Ramachandran.\n2. **Confirm Business Manager configuration** on the sandbox: site catalogue assignment (catalogue IDs to be confirmed against the sandbox, see the caveat in 3.1.8), storefront category tree, pricebook assignment per site/currency, and a search index rebuild so `shopper-search` returns results.\n3. **Verify SCAPI reachability** from the sandbox with a SLAS guest token and a `shopper-search` smoke test, to confirm data is queryable before front-end work starts.\n4. **Front-end proceeds via** `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` hooks against the populated sandbox: no code change is needed once data exists.\n5. **Track the permanent feeds** (SFCC-121) separately; the workaround load is throwaway once the permanent product and price feeds are delivering.\n\n5. Definition of Done: status\n-----------------------------\n\n> **DoD:** A documented inventory of relevant MRT APIs is produced and shared with the squad, sufficient to unblock BM configuration and front-end development in lower environments.\n\n| DoD element | Status |\n| --- | --- |\n| Inventory of relevant MRT/SCAPI APIs (endpoints, structure, payload, auth, data) | Done, section 3.1 |\n| Assessment of what can serve product/category/pricing in lower envs | Done, section 3.2 |\n| Limitations and gaps for MuleSoft to cover | Done, section 3.3 |\n| Permanent vs workaround classification | Done, section 3.4 |\n| Actions sufficient to unblock front-end dev | Done, section 4 (proven SDK/hook path; no code change once data exists) |\n| Actions sufficient to unblock BM config | Partial, section 4; the exact catalogue IDs and current sandbox data state are open questions for M. Ramachandran (section 6) |\n| Shared with the squad | Pending: this draft to be reviewed, then published to Confluence |\n\n6. Open questions\n-----------------\n\n1. What product / category / price data (if any) is currently loaded in the `bkzk-002` sandbox, and how did it get there?\n2. What are the actual catalogue IDs on the sandbox (master and per-site storefront)? The TSD names them `zimmermann-catalog` and `zimmermann-<site>-storefront-catalog`; please confirm these are correct for the sandbox.\n3. Who owns the SFCC cartridge repo and the sample/seed catalogue data, and can we get access to run an import?\n4. Preferred sandbox load mechanism for the interim: OCAPI Data API, BM site-archive import, or manual BM entry?\n5. Is the base BM config (site catalogue assignment, pricebook assignment, search index) already complete on the sandbox, or is any of it outstanding?\n6. Confirmed delivery mechanism and trigger for the permanent AP21 to MuleSoft to SFCC catalogue and price feed (ties to SFCC-121).\n\nAppendix A: Config reference (verified in code)\n-----------------------------------------------\n\n| Item | Value / location |\n| --- | --- |\n| PWA Kit runtime | `@salesforce/pwa-kit-runtime` / `-react-sdk` 3.18.0 (transitive via the base template) |\n| Base template | `@salesforce/retail-react-app` 10.0.0 (direct devDependency; template extensibility, `overrides/`) |\n| Commerce SDK | `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` 5.2.0 (transitive) |\n| Commerce API params | `config/default.js:130-138` |\n| Proxy configs | `config/default.js:208-217` (`api` to SCAPI, `ocapi` to sandbox) |\n| SSR / SLAS private client | `overrides/app/ssr.js:52` |\n| SCAPI host (Dev) | `qmyt7hks.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com` |\n| OCAPI host (Dev) | `bkzk-002.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com` |\n| Org / site (Dev) | `f_ecom_bkzk_002` / `ZimmermannAU` |\n| Sites | 10 PWA sites, 7 distinct SFCC sites (`config/sites.overlay.js`) |\n| Secrets | Held as MRT env vars / local `.env` (gitignored); never in the browser bundle |\n\nNote: the three `@salesforce/*` runtime and SDK packages are resolved transitively through `@salesforce/retail-react-app`; only the base template is pinned as a direct devDependency, so those versions can move on a template bump.\n\nAppendix B: Sources\n-------------------\n\n* Codebase (`zimmermann-pwa`): `.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md`, `.docs/integration/03-mulesoft.md`, `config/default.js`, `config/*.js`, `config/sites.overlay.js`, `overrides/app/ssr.js`, `overrides/app/components/_app-config/index.tsx`, `overrides/app/pages/home/index.tsx`, `overrides/app/ssr/connectionPools.ts`, `package.json`.\n* Confluence (space SFCC): \"Technical Solution Design, PWA\" (256835585), \"TSD: Product, SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration\" (292061208), \"TSD: Price, SFCC Pricebooks & Global-e\" (292388871), \"MuleSoft Integration, Open Questions for SFCC / PWA Design\" (320602113), \"SFCC Build and Deployment Process, Headless Architecture\" (264896514).\n* Jira (project SFCC): SFCC-122, SFCC-121, SFCC-123, SFCC-1.",
