{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "339935324",
    "title": "12. CDN, eCDN & Security Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339935324",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\neCDN, WAF, and security configuration in BM protects Zimmermann's storefronts and controls CDN caching behaviour. Two significant platform-level changes are relevant for a new SFCC build: the migration from WAFv1 to WAFv2, and the disabling of the deprecated Storefront Toolkit. Both have security implications if left unconfigured.\n\n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [eCDN Configuration in Business Manager](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/CDN/CDNConfiguration.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [Log Center Overview](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/OperationalInsights/LogCenter.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [B2C Commerce 25.7 Release Notes — Storefront Toolkit](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/ReleaseNotes/ReleaseNotes25_7.html)  \n**📎 Accenture Observability Deck:** See the Observability, Tracing & Security Assurance deck in this space for the shared responsibility model.\n\n**⚠️ Platform change (July 2025, v25.7):** The deprecated Storefront Toolkit is now **disabled by default** on all new and imported sites. If it was inadvertently re-enabled, disable it immediately.\n\n---\n\nChecklist\n---------\n\n### eCDN & WAF Configuration\n\nincompleteeCDN WAFv2 configured — confirm not still on legacy WAFv1 (self-service migration available in BM)\nincompleteCDN zone configured for each production storefront domain\nincompleteCustom hostnames registered with eCDN-managed TLS certificates (auto-renewing)\nincompleteProduction instances are **not** using `demandware.net` or hyphenated hostnames for public traffic — vanity hostname must be used\nincompleteProxy zone created in staging instances if needed (for eCDN certificate management)\n\n### Storefront Toolkit\n\nincompleteDeprecated Storefront Toolkit is **disabled** on all sites (v25.7 default — verify it has not been re-enabled)\nincompleteConfirmed no storefront code depends on the deprecated toolkit\n\n### Security Headers (Accenture-configured — verify BM alignment)\n\nincompleteContent Security Policy (CSP) directives in BM align with Accenture's Helmet configuration\nincompleteHSTS (HTTP Strict Transport Security) enabled\nincompleteX-Frame-Options configured\nincompleteReferrer-Policy configured\n\n### Log Centre Configuration\n\nincompleteLog Centre accessible in BM (Administration → Operations → Log Center)\nincompleteLog Centre Streaming configured to route to the APM destination (New Relic — as recommended in the Observability deck)\nincompleteMRT request logs, error logs, and CDN logs confirmed streaming\nincompleteSLAS error logs confirmed available in Log Centre\n\n### SCAPI Caching\n\nincompleteSCAPI server-side web-tier caching is enabled (enabled by default for new zones provisioned after March 2024)\nincompleteSCAPI caching tested — confirm cached responses are correct and not serving wrong-locale content\n\n### Penetration Testing (Zimmermann responsibility)\n\nincompleteThird-party application-layer pen test scoped and vendor procured\nincompletePen test scope includes: PWA Kit application, SCAPI integration points, SLAS auth flows, custom API endpoints\nincompletePen test scheduled post-UAT, pre go-live\nincompleteRepeat pen test planned 6 months post-launch\n\n\n---\n\nNotes / Findings\n----------------\n\n*Record gaps, decisions, and owner for remediation here.*\n\n| Finding | Severity | Owner | Resolved |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |  |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f6e1-fe0f",
    "page_width": "full-width"
  }
}"}

